# Rewrites for the routes that are NOT prerendered (/:lang/benefits, /:lang/start/*) to the
# empty SPA shell, spa.html. Status 200 (a rewrite, not a redirect) so the URL is preserved.
#
# Keep these rules narrow. Cloudflare Pages applies _redirects BEFORE static files, so a
# catch-all such as `/* /spa 200` would serve the empty shell in place of every prerendered page
# and quietly destroy the SEO the prerendering exists for. (The old `/* /index.html 200` only
# seemed harmless because Pages ignores that exact rule as a loop.) The target is written /spa,
# not /spa.html: a .html target makes Pages answer with a 308 instead.
#
# Any other unknown path falls through to Pages' built-in fallback, index.html (the home page),
# and the app sends it on to the right language.
/en/benefits  /spa  200
/en/start/*  /spa  200
/nl/benefits  /spa  200
/nl/start/*  /spa  200
/fr/benefits  /spa  200
/fr/start/*  /spa  200
/de/benefits  /spa  200
/de/start/*  /spa  200
